    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d707">

                <pb facs="1007" n="901" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg901"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00111 <hi rendition="#superscript">Armament
                        Control/Military Secrets</hi>/2364</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Controls</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Green</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-11-28">November 28, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. William Francis Gibbs, of Gibbs &amp;
                    Cox, Inc., naval architects, called me by telephone from New York this
                    afternoon. He said that <pb facs="1008" n="902" xml:id="pg902"/> he proposed to
                    send a copy of the Department’s letter of November 18, 1939, to the
                    representatives of the U. S. S. R.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d707-f1"/> with whom he
                    had been dealing in connection with the proposal to have vessels of war
                    constructed in this country for the Soviet Government. He asked whether I
                    perceived any objection to his communicating a copy of that letter to
                    representatives of the U. S. S. R.</p>
                <p>I replied in the negative.</p>
                <p>Mr. Gibbs said that all he wanted now was
                    “to give the project a decent burial”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph C. Green</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d707-f1" n="16" xml:id="d707-f1-content">
                <p>This letter was quoted in a communication of November 28, 1939, to the Soviet
                    Naval Mission and the Amtorg Trading Corporation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
